WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.251
When all the hype for Logan began way back
in March 2015, Hugh Jackman tweeted that it

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:07.790
would be his "last time putting on the claws."

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.570
Given how many times Jackman has donned the
adamantium claws and played the scrappiest

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:16.070
mutant in the X-Universe, it's no wonder that
he's finally ready to step away from the role.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.950
But his departure opens up a very big question
that's on every superhero movie fan's mind:

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.690
who should play Wolverine after Jackman?

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:27.040
While it seems plausible that Fox could cast
a relatively unknown actor, there's just as

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.980
good a chance we'll see a more established
actor pick up the claws.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.899
While you might not agree with some of these
ideas for replacements, but there's a chance

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:36.570
that one of them could be the next Wolverine.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.739
Tom Hardy

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:41.650
Here's the man who's got the best possible
positioning going into this discussion: Hugh

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.199
Jackman actually said outright, "I think Tom
Hardy would be a great Wolverine."

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:50.339
Of course, that's assuming that Hardy would
actually want to be Wolverine, since at this

00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:53.359
point he pretty much has his pick of any movie
he wants.

00:00:53.359 --> 00:00:57.100
At the very least, though, there's no question
that you'd get some fantastic acting out of

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.139
Logan if Hardy were to play the part.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.070
Just look at whatever this is!

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.160
"Right, that's enough! He's had enough. Get him out of here!"

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.980
Liam Hemsworth

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.000
We already know that playing comic book heroes
runs in the Hemsworth family, so why not make

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.130
Liam Logan?

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.480
As it stands right now, though, Thor and Wolverine
aren't in the same movie universes anyway,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.060
so the family resemblance might never actually
be an issue should he get the role.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.100
But Liam's clearly proven his chops as an
action hero already, so kicking things up

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.820
a notch and giving him a chance to play Wolverine
wouldn't be out of the question for this rising

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.210
action star.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:30.210
Kit Harington

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:34.110
Sure, Harington's got a lot on his plate,
what with Game of Thrones and all.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:38.010
But when the series has run its course, it'll
probably be right about time for someone else

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.930
to step in and take over for Jackman.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:44.220
We already know that he's capable of being
a badass, and he's about as high-profile an

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.160
actor as 20th Century Fox could hope to get
in the role.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.740
It's win-win for everyone!

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.840
Penn Badgley

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.930
The former Gossip Girl star hasn't managed
to secure a real breakout role since wrapping

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:57.750
up his run as Dan Humphrey, but for those
who've been paying attention, he's been turning

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.840
critics' heads in such films as Greetings
from Tim Buckley, Cymbeline, and The Paper

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.390
Store while also fronting the band MOTHXR.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.660
Not that we're discouraging the man from his
music career, but this is the sort of role

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.960
that might lead him to drop the mic and step
back in front of the camera full-time.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.190
Taylor Kitsch

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:17.620
After proving his mettle in almost 70 episodes
of NBC's Friday Night Lights, Taylor Kitsch

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.140
played the lead role in back-to-back bombs
John Carter and Battleship.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.790
But even before those flops, he had a shot
at entering the X-Universe by playing Gambit

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.110
in X-Men Origins: Wolverine.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:31.569
That role didn't work out much better for
Kitsch than John Carter did, but he's shown

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:34.670
that, with a capable director, he can hold
his own on the silver screen.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:38.640
And besides, we've already seen Chris Evans
successfully hop from one Marvel superhero

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.030
to another, while Ryan Reynolds redeemed himself
by taking another crack at Deadpool.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:47.070
After those two superhero successes, Kitsch
getting the claws might not be as crazy as

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.200
it sounds.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.340
Ryan Kwanten

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.959
Given the amount of success that came with
an Australian in the role last time, it couldn't

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:55.240
hurt to consider another Ozzie this time around.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.780
The former True Blood star Ryan Kwanten could
definitely fit the bill.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.410
He's done his fair share of action films,
including Blunt Force Trauma and Northmen:

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.530
A Viking Saga.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:07.800
If he seems like a left-field choice, well,
just consider how much you knew about Hugh

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.060
Jackman before the first X-Men film.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.520
Exactly.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:16.770
Jared Padalecki

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:21.970
There's no way The CW is going to keep Supernatural
going much longer, which means that Sam Winchester's

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:26.100
Jared Padalecki is going to be out of a job
at some point in the relatively near future.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.670
He's proven that he can battle back against
the forces of evil on repeated occasions,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.340
so he's already got that aspect of the character
down.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.810
If he can just get past all those years of
working alongside Jensen Ackles and get in

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.510
the habit of playing a lone wolf, he'll be
perfect.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.520
Aidan Turner

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.660
He's played a vampire on Being Human, a dwarf
in The Hobbit, and since then he's been busy

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.349
as the title character on PBS's Poldark, but
Aidan Turner hasn't yet had the chance to

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:49.590
play a superhero.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.800
He has, however, received acclaim for his
performances in all three of those projects,

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.660
so why not give him a chance to brandish a
set of adamantium claws and really go for

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.660
broke?

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.660
Alex O'Loughlin

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.530
Okay, we know Alex O'Loughlin is a little
bit older than the other options, but there's

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.140
nothing that says that he can't play Wolverine
into his fifties.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.580
He's done the vampire thing on Moonlight,
and he's been playing a cop for many seasons

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:14.340
now on CBS's Hawaii Five-0 reboot, so we know
he can be dark, brooding, and play the bad

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.150
cop when the need arises.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.380
William Levy

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:21.290
Although Cuban-American actor William Levy
is better known for his work in telenovelas

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:25.410
and his stint on Dancing with the Stars than
he is action films, 2016 saw him show up in

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.600
two such films — Term Life and Resident
Evil: The Final Chapter — and he's also

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.320
been cast in Brent Ryan Green's post-apocalyptic
flick The Veil.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.590
As long as he keeps up this kind of work,
he's got a good shot at being considered for

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.590
the role.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.020
Joe Manganiello

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.340
Joe Manganiello just turned 40, but he's still
got the look, the swagger, and the requisite

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.560
sense of humor to kick ass as Wolverine.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.340
Manganiello is a veteran of the sci-fi/fantasy
genre after his years on True Blood, and if

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.740
you've never seen that, you'll probably recognize
him best as this guy from the original Spider-Man.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.990
Plus, he's been cast as Deathstroke in The
Batman.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.500
Could there be a more perfect candidate?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.660
Scott Eastwood

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.180
Given how easy it would've been to imagine
his dad Clint stepping into the role of Old

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:09.260
Man Logan a couple of years ago, the father-son
resemblance between the two makes it pretty

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:13.190
easy to picture Scott Eastwood popping out
a pair of claws and giving super villains

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.190
the business.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.610
He's also been known to chomp on a cigar on
occasion, which puts him even closer to Logan

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.710
territory without even trying.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.710
Daniel Radcliffe

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.050
Okay, stick with us here, but Harry Potter
might actually be a viable possibility to

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.050
play Logan.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.460
"Oh God, I've still got these on?

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.510
I don't need these.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.820
They're just for the character."

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:30.820
No, seriously!

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:34.640
Some people might be skeptical even now, but
he's been working out and expanding his range,

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.520
and with films like Horns and Imperium, it's
no longer out of the realm of possibility

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.550
that he could plausibly play a badass.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:44.850
Yeah, okay, maybe he's a little skinny for
the role, but he's clearly capable of growing

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:48.100
the requisite facial hair, and given that
there's photographic evidence that he has

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:52.070
at least some muscles, it isn't hard to picture
him bulking up even further if the opportunity

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.240
presented itself.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.740
And before you dismiss any of these possibilities,
just remember: before he became Wolverine,

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.199
Hugh Jackman was best known for his work in
musicals as a song and dance kinda guy.

00:06:02.199 --> 00:06:06.360
Not only that, but Wolverine has always been
known as a short character, but Jackman is

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.370
pretty dang tall at six-foot-two.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.600
Don't count anyone out when it comes to searching
for the new Wolverine, okay?

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.600
Even Harry Potter!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.180
After all, if Radcliffe could pull off this
look, why not Wolverine?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.550
Thanks for watching!

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.040
Clip the Looper icon to subscribe to our YouTube
channel.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.300
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too.

